.TH WINO-MAIL 1 "" "Wino Mail" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wino-mail \- mail, calendar, contacts and To Do
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wino-mail
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fIFILE\fR|\fIURI\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Wino Mail is a mail client with a calendar, contacts and To Do. It works with Outlook, Gmail, IMAP and Exchange
accounts, and with calendars and address books over CalDAV and CardDAV.
.PP
Only one instance runs per user; a second start hands its options and files to the running one.
Files (\fI.eml\fR messages) and \fImailto:\fR or \fIwino:\fR addresses given on the command line are opened.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-compose
Open a new message.
.TP
.B \-\-new\-event
Open a new calendar event.
.TP
.BI \-\-mode " mode"
Open the app in \fImail\fR, \fIcalendar\fR, \fIcontacts\fR or \fItodo\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start without a window, as the launch at sign-in setting does. The window opens on the next start.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/wino-mail
Accounts, messages and settings. Removing the package keeps them.
.PP
The protection key of the stored credentials is kept in the Secret Service (GNOME Keyring).
.SH SEE ALSO
https://www.winomail.app
